/*
 * Shared test fixture — not shipped in any package.
 *
 * A real Frontier journal `Loadout` event for an engineered combat fit of the Anaconda Mk II:
 * gimballed beam lasers, two large torpedo pylons, eight shield boosters, a size-8 Prismatic
 * shield generator, two shield cell banks and grade-5 engineering on almost every module. Each
 * `Engineering` block states the `OriginalValue` the game holds for the stock module.
 *
 * The two module reinforcement packages are Mercenary articles raised to grade 5. The stock
 * package has no engineering menu. They state their protection as `ModuleDefenceAbsorption`.
 *
 * It is the same ship (`ShipID` 224) as `journal-anaconda-mk-ii.jsonc`, refitted. The
 * corpus build `builds/anacondamkii-combat.jsonc` records the same fit.
 *
 * Contributed 2026-11-17 UTC by the repository owner from their own fleet, with no upstream
 * project. The pasted source line has SHA-256
 * `47d30ba25a798a1e6d2dc538415a1cbe45fd52055780b801e69d99c6f0b34fef`; the stored, re-indented
 * fixture has SHA-256 `200708e08430fcb338007bcac513a339bdf25f8f625b8c27b10a04400071f0e9`.
 *
 * `ShipName`, `ShipIdent`, `ShipID` and `timestamp` are kept — they describe a ship, and nothing
 * in the event names a person. The `Engineer` fields name the game's engineers.
 *
 * The capture is Elite Dangerous game output and remains the property of Frontier Developments
 * plc, redistributed under Frontier's media-usage terms; see ATTRIBUTIONS.md.
 *
 * A stored checksum here is of the payload alone, taken with this header comment removed; a source
 * checksum is of the upstream file as it was received.
 */
